.TH EXP 3
.SH NAME
exp, log, log10, pow, sqrt \- exponential, logarithm, power, square root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <math.h>

double
exp(x)
double x;

double
log(x)
double x;

double
log10(x)
double x;

double
pow(x, y)
double x, y;

double
sqrt(x)
double x;
.fi
.PP
cc ... \-lm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B exp
returns the exponential function of
.IR x ,
e to the power
.IR x .
.PP
.B log
returns the natural logarithm of
.IR x ,
and
.B log10
the logarithm to base 10.
.PP
.B pow
returns
.I x
to the power
.IR y .
.PP
.B sqrt
returns the square root of
.IR x .
.PP
.B sqrt
is correctly rounded, as is
.B log10
of a power of ten. pow of a whole number power is exact when the result
can be held exactly, as pow(2.0, 10.0) or pow(10.0, 22.0). The other
results are within one unit in the last place of the exact value.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.TP 12
.B exp
returns HUGE (an infinity) when the result is too large, and 0 when it
is too small.
.TP
.BR log ", " log10
of zero return \-HUGE, with a SING error; of a negative
.IR x ,
\-HUGE, with a DOMAIN error.
.TP
.B pow
of
.I x
zero and
.I y
zero or negative, or of
.I x
negative and
.I y
not a whole number, returns 0, with a DOMAIN error; when the result is
too large, HUGE or \-HUGE, and when it is too small, 0.
.TP
.B sqrt
of a negative
.I x
returns 0, with a DOMAIN error.
.PP
For a DOMAIN or SING error, a message such as "sqrt: DOMAIN error" is
written on the standard error. A program can handle the errors itself
with
.BR matherr (3).
.SH ERRORS
errno is set to EDOM after a DOMAIN or SING error, and to ERANGE when
the result is too large or too small.
.SH SEE ALSO
hypot(3), sinh(3), matherr(3), intro(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B exp
and
.B log
functions first appeared in Version 1 AT&T UNIX,
.B sqrt
in Version 2,
.B pow
in Version 3, and
.B log10
in Version 7.
